Yes, same things are checked.

> I downloaded the 3.4.3 source, used the latest versions of all the patches
> available to me (all 3.4.3 or 3.4.2 versions) spent some time making sure
> everything got patched right, set up my makefile and config file, compiled,
> and tried to load a saved game.
> "Configuration incompatibility for file "C:\nethack\<name of the save file>"

Compare your include/config.h files of the two versions. There must be
something different. For example the options TEXTCOLOR, SCORE_ON_BOTL and
EXP_ON_BOTL are among the ones checked.. the others are on by default so
you probably didn't change them, but SCORE_ON_BOTL is off by default, so
if you turned it on, you need to have it also defined in IGNORED_FEATURES
in util/makedefs.c to keep the files.
Or maybe you have MAIL compiled in on one version and not in the other?

You could get the nhidsave utility from
http://www.nethack.de/programs.shtml to check the magic numbers of the
3.4.2 save file. Then, start a new game with 3.4.3, save it and see what's
different. 

> I tried directly copying my config.h from 3.4.2 to the 3.4.3
> directories,

Directly copying config.h is not a good idea, because there may be
something that needs to be different, new settings that must be there for
the game to compile correctly (I haven't checked if there is something
like that).

